Platform packages include the Tcl 8.6 runtime and standard scripts.
Tcl, zlib and LibTomMath license texts are included in bin/tcl/.
Tcl source: https://github.com/tcltk/tcl/tree/core-8-6-18

Platform packages include LuaJIT through the mlua Rust binding.
The LuaJIT license and bundled Lua notices are in licenses/LuaJIT.txt.

The RTL schematic webview includes elkjs 0.12.1 under EPL-2.0.
The license is in licenses/ELK.md. The corresponding source is available at
https://github.com/kieler/elkjs/tree/v0.12.1.

Linux x64 packages include Ondas under Apache-2.0, with runtime SDK loading
changes in https://github.com/AndreaFrederica/ondas/tree/wave-workbench-sdk.
The license is in licenses/Ondas-Apache-2.0.txt.

The Rust PSFXL reader includes C-Blosc 1.21.6 through blosc-src.
The C-Blosc license is in licenses/C-Blosc-BSD-3-Clause.txt.
The LZ4, Snappy, zlib and Zstandard licenses are in licenses/PSFXL-Compression.txt.
The Rust LZ4 block decoder includes lz4_flex under the MIT license.
The license is in licenses/Lz4-flex-MIT.txt.

The Rust PSF reader includes psfkit under the MIT license.
The license is in licenses/Psfkit-MIT.txt. Source: https://github.com/henjo/polars-psf.

The Tcl Console bundles Monaco Editor 0.57.0 under the MIT license.
The license is included in dist/monaco-editor-license.txt.
Source: https://github.com/microsoft/monaco-editor/tree/v0.57.0.
